{"nodes": [{"id": "memory_query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c_extraction_artifact_finding", "label": "24-Community Bridge Is an Extraction Artifact", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "graphify-out/memory/query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-11T14:10:06.954821+00:00", "author": null, "contributor": "graphify", "rationale": "The apparent bridging of 24 communities by core_defaultfailoverstore (type=concept, source=docs/adr/adr.md, degree=108) is not real architecture \u2014 it is a fuzzy-dedup collapse of at least three distinct classes into one node."}, {"id": "memory_query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c_fuzzy_dedup_collapse", "label": "Fuzzy Dedup Collapse", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "graphify-out/memory/query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-11T14:10:06.954821+00:00", "author": null, "contributor": "graphify", "rationale": "The merge step reported 908 deduplicated nodes, 404 of them fuzzy; core_defaultfailoverstore is one of them, absorbing the store class, the JDBC query resolver, and DefaultFailoverHandler's method surface plus a false 'implements FailoverHandler' edge."}, {"id": "memory_query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c_defaultfailoverstore", "label": "DefaultFailoverStore", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "graphify-out/memory/query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c.md", "source_location": "failover-core/core/store", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-11T14:10:06.954821+00:00", "author": null, "contributor": "graphify", "rationale": "Implements FailoverStore and FailoverStoreSizeAware with exactly seven methods: store, delete, find, findAll, cleanByExpiry, liveEntryCount, liveEntryCountSupported. It does NOT implement FailoverHandler."}, {"id": "memory_query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c_defaultfailoverstorequeryresolver", "label": "DefaultFailoverStoreQueryResolver (Absorbed Node)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "graphify-out/memory/query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c.md", "source_location": "failover-store-jdbc/resolver", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-11T14:10:06.954821+00:00", "author": null, "contributor": "graphify", "rationale": "Owns validateTablePrefix, resolveMergeQuery, applyPrefix, buildInsertMergeTypes, buildUpdateTypes, DatabaseResolver and PayloadColumnResolver, yet has zero nodes of its own in the graph \u2014 it was entirely absorbed into core_defaultfailoverstore."}, {"id": "memory_query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c_defaultfailoverhandler", "label": "DefaultFailoverHandler (Split Across 3 Nodes)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "graphify-out/memory/query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-11T14:10:06.954821+00:00", "author": null, "contributor": "graphify", "rationale": "Its recover, recoverAll, doRecover and clean surface was partly absorbed into core_defaultfailoverstore, while the class itself resolves to three separate nodes \u2014 the inverse of the collapse defect."}, {"id": "memory_query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c_failoverstorejdbc", "label": "FailoverStoreJdbc (Split Across 5 Nodes)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "graphify-out/memory/query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-11T14:10:06.954821+00:00", "author": null, "contributor": "graphify", "rationale": "Resolves to five separate graph nodes under inconsistent ID schemes; AdvancedFailoverHandler likewise resolves to three."}, {"id": "memory_query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c_node_id_scheme_violation", "label": "Inconsistent Node ID Scheme", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "graphify-out/memory/query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-11T14:10:06.954821+00:00", "author": null, "contributor": "graphify", "rationale": "Duplicate class nodes carry inconsistent IDs including at least one full-path ID that violates the parent_dir_filename_entity rule, which is what lets the same class split into several nodes."}, {"id": "memory_query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c_god_node_distortion", "label": "God-node Degree and Betweenness Distortion", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "graphify-out/memory/query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-11T14:10:06.954821+00:00", "author": null, "contributor": "graphify", "rationale": "Because collapse inflates degree and splitting deflates it, god-node rankings and betweenness-derived questions in GRAPH_REPORT.md partly measure dedup damage rather than real coupling. Remedy: graphify extract --force to rebuild IDs cleanly."}], "edges": [{"source": "memory_query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c_extraction_artifact_finding", "target": "memory_query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c_fuzzy_dedup_collapse", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "graphify-out/memory/query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "memory_query_20260811_141006_why_does_defaultfailoverstore_bridge_24_separate_c_fuzzy_dedup_collapse", "ta